body:
System settings pages (Users, Orgs, Roles, Permissions, Audit Log) used hand-written HTML tables with manual fetch/CRUD logic, duplicating ~500 lines of nearly identical code across 5 files. Replaced with the platform's `ObjectView` from `@object-ui/plugin-view`, driven by existing `systemObjects.ts` metadata.

### Changes

- **New `SystemObjectViewPage` component** — shared wrapper that builds an `ObjectViewSchema` from `systemObjects.ts` definitions and renders `ObjectView` with the adapter dataSource
- **All 5 management pages** now delegate to `SystemObjectViewPage` (~25 lines each, down from ~140)
  - CRUD gated by `isAdmin` via `operations` config
  - Audit log uses `readOnly` mode
  - Search, sort, filter, pagination come free from ObjectView
- **Tests updated** — mock `@object-ui/plugin-view` and assert schema props (objectName, operations, columns) rather than testing hand-rolled table rendering

```tsx
// Before: 144 lines of useState, useCallback, fetch, hand-written <table>
// After:
export function UserManagementPage() {
  const { user } = useAuth();
  return (
    <SystemObjectViewPage
      objectName="sys_user"
      title="User Management"
      description="Manage system users and their roles"
      icon={Users}
      isAdmin={user?.role === 'admin'}
    />
  );
}
```

22 system page tests pass, 750 total console tests pass. CHANGELOG.md and ROADMAP.md updated.

